# Release and Operations

Before release, consider:
- Environment/configuration parity and secret availability.
- Build and test results.
- Database migration order, compatibility and rollback/forward-fix.
- Health checks, logs, metrics and alerting.
- Background jobs, queues, scheduled tasks and webhook behavior.
- Backups and restore readiness for data-impacting releases.
- Feature flags, staged rollout and rollback plan.
- User-facing changes, support notes and documentation.

Never deploy, push, publish or alter production resources without explicit user authorization.
